# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored. No exchange keys are used anywhere.
# Only needed to call Jev yourself (python -m jevtrade.collect / jevtrade.decision);
# the hourly collect workflow reads it from the OPENROUTER_API_KEY repository secret:
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# The API's "Jev forward log" reads the data-log branch from GitHub. Needed if the
# repo is private (read-only "Contents" access is enough); also lifts rate limits:
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# With "Actions: read and write" too, JEVTRADE_KICK=1 starts the hourly collect run
# whenever GitHub's schedule skips an hour (see docs/deploy.md).
